    turnFlow: 'Each game has four stages: (1) Dressing the board—each player places one chip in each of the seven compartments (Ás, Kongur, Drottning, Gosi, Tía, Pamfíll, and central Púkk). (2) Collecting the ante—the turned card designates trump; holders of the Ace, King, Queen, Jack or Ten of trump collect the corresponding pool; the holder of Pamfíll (Jack of Clubs) collects that pool (and both if clubs are trump). (3) Að Púkka—in turn, each player may add a chip to the Púkk compartment to enter; Pamfíll is wild for hand ranking; hands are five of a kind, four, three, or pair (sixes beat Aces); wagering one chip at a time until two remain or no raises; showdown and highest hand wins the Púkk pot. (4) Playing out the hand—shedding: left of dealer leads; players follow with same suit one rank higher until Ace or no one can follow; last to play in a sequence starts the next; first to empty hand wins; others pay one chip per card left.',
